[2026-08-11] CONTENT BACKEND — Payload CMS (external)
└── Blute site content is no longer purely static. LinkedIn posts are authored in a Payload CMS
    instance deployed separately on Vercel and consumed by the Angular app over REST.
    ├── Admin UI  -> https://payload-nine-ivory.vercel.app/admin
    ├── REST base -> https://payload-nine-ivory.vercel.app/api/<collection>
    ├── Config    -> src/environments/environment.ts (payloadBaseUrl, payloadPostsCollection)
    ├── Service   -> src/app/services/linkedin-posts.service.ts
    │   └── normalizePost() tolerates varying Payload field names; if the CMS schema changes,
    │       update the candidate key arrays there rather than the components.
    ├── Consumers -> src/app/latest-posts (home strip, 3 posts) and src/app/insights (/insights listing)
    ├── Card UI   -> src/app/shared/post-card/post-card.component.ts (shared by both consumers)
    └── Read access on the collection must stay PUBLIC in Payload access control,
        otherwise the browser receives an empty docs array with no error.

